Wyreup replaces UUID v4 generation with the platform cryptographic API and
rebuilds the browser distribution from verified source with audited dependencies.
StreamBuf.pipe returns its destination, preserving the standard stream contract
required by the upgraded archiver dependency used for streaming XLSX output.
The browser bundle's constituent package versions and license texts appear in
vendor/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt and vendor/BROWSER-DEPENDENCIES.json.
The streaming workbook reader uses unzipper's native async iterator to preserve all file-backed archive entries with the updated unzipper dependency.
The Node streaming workbook writer uses a bundled Archiver 7.0.1 factory with
glob 14.0.2 and minimatch 11.0.1. Its complete package/input/manifest/license
provenance and license texts are in vendor/NODE-DEPENDENCIES.json,
vendor/NODE-METAFILE.json and vendor/NODE-THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt.
Consumer package-manager audits do not inspect this bundled code. A raw-zero
consumer audit is not a bundled-code security result; the full workspace audit
covers the exact bundled build dependencies, whose lock membership is verified.
The repository's glob 14.0.2 manifest patch selects its published unbundled
entries so the matcher and filesystem dependencies appear as individual inputs.
